MinGW portability for MesenCE's Core/Utilities (FujiNet Go NES builds Mesen's
C++ core with mingw-w64 -- MSYS2 UCRT64 in CI, and cross from Linux).

- UTF8Util.h: open streams with const wchar_t* (decode().c_str()); the
  std::wstring overload is MSVC-only, and every libstdc++ has the pointer one.
- UTF8Util.cpp: the Win32 UTF-8 decode was guarded by _MSC_VER, so MinGW
  threw "utf8::decode is not implemented" on the first file open.
- Lower-case Windows SDK header names (<windows.h>, <ws2tcpip.h>,
  <versionhelpers.h>, <d3d9.h>): mingw-w64's headers live on a
  case-sensitive filesystem when cross-compiling.
- PlatformUtilities.cpp: include <mmsystem.h> for timeBeginPeriod, which a
  WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN windows.h leaves out.
- UPnPPortMapper.cpp: mingw-w64 has no natupnp.h; UPnP is only used by
  netplay, so MinGW gets the existing non-Windows stub.

Apply in a MesenCE checkout with: git apply mesen-mingw.patch

